This is not a toy app. It is structured like a real product architecture and is already close to a production-ready MVP for outbound voice qualification.

9. Important Points to Preserve in Antigravity
When continuing this project, the following should not be removed or changed casually:

zero-Redis design
PostgreSQL as system-of-record
per-call attempt isolation
Twilio + ElevenLabs + LLM pipeline
status-driven lead lifecycle
websocket-based live updates
backend worker queue pattern
callback logic tied to timezone-aware scheduling
10. Recommended Next-Step Direction
For continuation under Antigravity, the next phase should focus on:

Stability and reliability

monitor failed webhook flows
verify status callback reliability
improve idempotency handling for repeated webhooks
Better production resilience

add stronger error classification
improve retry safety
tighten timeout handling
Product polish

refine lead qualification workflow
improve agent prompt quality
strengthen callback logic and scheduling experience
Scale-readiness

optimize query patterns
add better indexing
review queue performance and throughput
11. Final Summary
This project already has the core of a real AI-driven sales qualification platform:

inbound lead capture
outbound voice calling
AI conversational flow
qualification engine
callback scheduling
admin dashboard
live real-time telemetry
The system architecture is sound and coherent.

The key idea is that the backend orchestrates a full call lifecycle using PostgreSQL, Twilio, ElevenLabs, and an LLM layer, while the frontend remains a thin live dashboard over that operational backend.

This is a strong base for continuation, and the correct architectural direction is to keep the same design patterns rather than rebuilding from scratch.

